5. Make the frontend resilient
   The UI should handle:

empty file upload
invalid FASTA
network/API failures
unsupported antibiotic
missing model metadata
slow prediction times
This is the user-facing side of operational stability.

6. Add tests before deployment
   Start with:

unit tests for metadata loading
unit tests for active feature intersection on a mock or saved vector
API tests for /api/v1/predict
one end-to-end test with a valid FASTA and one invalid FASTA
This is the difference between “works on my machine” and “deployment-ready”.

7. Add environment and deployment config
   You will want:

.env or environment variables for ports, model paths, CORS origins
separate dev/prod settings
health checks
logs
secure file handling
For deployment, keep the backend config in one place instead of hardcoding paths.

8. Install and verify external runtime dependencies
   Ensure production environment has:

BLAST installed and in PATH
KMC available and executable
Python dependencies installed exactly
compatible versions of lightgbm, joblib, numpy, pandas, scikit-learn, fastapi, uvicorn
I would also pin versions in a requirements file to avoid runtime drift.

9. Containerize it
   For deployment, Docker is the best next step.

Recommended minimal setup:

one container for the FastAPI backend
one container for the Vite frontend, or serve static build output via a lightweight server
optionally a reverse proxy like Nginx
This makes cloud deployment much easier.

10. Choose a deployment target
    Good options for this app:

Azure App Service
Azure Container Apps
Render
Railway
Fly.io
AWS ECS / Elastic Beanstalk
If this is an MVP:

simplest: deploy backend on Azure/Render
frontend: static hosting on Vercel or Netlify
API: backend on Render/Azure
Recommended implementation order
Real model artifact validation
Fill metadata
Validate actual prediction endpoint
Add tests
Containerize
Deploy
My recommendation
The app is close to being functionally complete, but it is not “fully operational” until:

real trained files exist
metadata matches the real models
end-to-end prediction is tested with real inputs
deployment config is locked down
If you want, I can produce the exact next-step checklist as a GitHub-style task list, or I can set up the deployment skeleton for the backend and frontend next.
